.TH DNS 1
.SH NAME
dns \- resolve hostnames over DNS-over-HTTPS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dns
.RB [ -6 ]
.RB [ -s
.IR resolver-ip ]
.RB [ -u
.IR resolver-url ]
.IR name ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Dns
resolves each
.I name
over DNS-over-HTTPS
.RI ( doh (2)),
printing a line
.RI \(lq name\ address \(rq
per address. Because it resolves over this tree's own TLS through a
resolver reached by literal IP, it needs no
.I /net/cs
and no host resolver \(em it is the first command in the tree that
can turn a name into an address by itself.
.PP
.B -6
asks for AAAA (IPv6) records instead of A.
.B -s
and
.B -u
point at a different DoH provider (its dial IP and its
.B /dns-query
URL); by default it uses Google Public DNS
.RB ( dns.google
at
.BR 8.8.8.8 ).
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/dns.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR doh (2),
.IR dohtest (1),
.IR dial (2),
.IR tls12 (2)
.SH BUGS
It resolves through one DoH provider (Google by default) with no
caching and no fallback, and is not yet wired into
.IR dial (2)'s
own name resolution \(em a caller (or a program) must run
.B dns
explicitly rather than dialling a name and having it resolve. Needs
the network and the provider reachable.
